cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata.
title: >-
  Security Passport: an evidence-backed operational passport for
  European financial instruments
authors:
  - name: Huntsman1756
    url: https://github.com/Huntsman1756
repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/Huntsman1756/security-passport
version: "0.2.1"
date-released: "2026-10-07"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - ISIN
  - capital markets
  - market infrastructure
  - post-trade
  - provenance
  - temporal queries
abstract: >-
  Security Passport turns an ISIN into an evidence-backed
  operational record. Every reported, derived, or inferred field
  carries provenance; blocks answer a requested --as-of date
  only from admissible evidence — unavailable historical
  evidence is never replaced with current knowledge.
